# MCP usage

Opt-in per task. **Ask once, wait for yes** before connecting — unless already approved this session. **Free tools only** unless the user asks otherwise. Every server is pinned to an exact version and runs isolated (`security.mdc`).

## Reference research: capture tool first

1. Run `node tools/capture.mjs` (skill `capture-reference`). It needs no MCP and is the hardened path.
2. Playwright MCP is for what the capture can't do: one sniper check on the live reference, interaction states, and our own build. Ask before activating it.
3. Never connect any browser MCP to the user's everyday browser or profile (no extension mode, no CDP endpoint).

Kickoff does **not** need a browser.

## Catalog

| MCP | When | Connect |
|---|---|---|
| **Playwright** | Sniper checks, states, our build, QA | `.cursor/mcp.json` → `@playwright/mcp@0.0.83 --isolated --block-service-workers` + `tools/playwright-mcp.config.json` (sandbox on, downloads off) |
| **Chrome DevTools** | Lighthouse / traces on the production URL | `npx -y chrome-devtools-mcp@1.10.1 --isolated` — never without `--isolated` |
| **shadcn** | Registry components | `npx -y shadcn@4.21.4 mcp` |
| **Context7** | Next / Tailwind / Sanity docs | `.cursor/mcp.json` → `@upstash/context7-mcp@4.3.0` |
| **Sanity** | After content model confirmed | Add `"sanity": { "url": "https://mcp.sanity.io" }` to `.cursor/mcp.json` when the content model is confirmed |
| **Cloudflare Docs** | Deploy / DNS / Workers docs | Add `"cloudflare-docs": { "url": "https://docs.mcp.cloudflare.com/mcp" }` to `.cursor/mcp.json` when needed |
| **Cloudflare API / Builds** | Only if the user asks | Take the URL from Cloudflare's own developer docs, never from search results; use a scoped API token, never the global key |

Pins come from the coordinator (checked 2026-10-27, each at least two weeks old); change them only in the kit, never in a project. Never install lookalike or "wrapper" packages. `.cursor/mcp.json` has no "disabled" field: project servers appear in Cursor's MCP settings — keep them switched off there until a task needs one.

Optional extras (only if the user asks): A1 Gallery, Firecrawl.

## Phase defaults

| Phase | Use | Skip |
|---|---|---|
| Kickoff | none | all |
| Scaffold | Context7 | design refs, deploy |
| Industry research | capture tool → Playwright (sniper only) | Sanity create, deploy, Lighthouse |
| Design system | Context7 | deploy |
| Build | shadcn → capture `--local` → overlay + measure-diff tools | Lighthouse every section; deploy |
| CMS | Sanity + Context7 | design-ref MCPs |
| Design QA | capture + overlay tools → Chrome DevTools (isolated) | shadcn |
| Deploy / host | preship-scrub → Cloudflare Docs | design-ref MCPs |

## Rules

1. Need → ask → connect → use.
2. Prefer already-connected tools.
3. No Sanity project/schema while `[REQUIRED]` remain or before the content model is confirmed.
4. No API keys in rules, MCP config or git.
5. Don't duplicate this catalog into `plan.md`.
6. `node tools/scan-kit.mjs` must show no HIGH after any MCP change.
